litepdf local patch to MuPDF 1.27.2: one-pass outline resolve for HTML-engine documents
=======================================================================================

Marker:   LITEPDF_PATCH_HTDOC_OUTLINE_V1
Date:     2026-11-12
Issue:    https://github.com/jeffchen1981-fu/litepdf/issues/229
Applied:  by cmake/ImportMuPDF.cmake at configure time (git apply), when
          source/html/html-doc.c does not carry the marker.

What it changes
---------------
source/html/html-doc.c only. htdoc_update_outline, which htdoc_layout runs
after every layout, resolved each outline entry with htdoc_resolve_link,
one fz_find_html_target walk of the whole box tree per entry. An FB2 book
has one entry per section title, so N titles cost O(N^2): 7.2 s of a 7.6 s
page count for a 1,500-section book (#229). The patch walks the box tree
once in find_box_target's order, records the first y for each id in an
fz_tree, and resolves each entry from it. An entry whose first match is not
at y >= 0, or every entry when building the index fails, goes through
htdoc_resolve_link as before, so every entry gets exactly the position it
got before. htdoc_resolve_link itself (link following) is unchanged.

It also defines litepdf_mupdf_patch_notice_v1, the modification notice
(AGPL-3.0 section 5(a)) that litepdf shows in its About box. Referencing it
makes a library built without this patch version fail litepdf's link.

The patch copies find_first_content and the value rules of
find_box_target / find_flow_target from source/html/html-outline.c, which
it does not touch; ImportMuPDF.cmake checks that file's hash so a MuPDF
bump that changes those rules stops the configure.

Changing this patch: regenerate it with `git diff --output=<file> --
source/html/html-doc.c` from the MuPDF root, bump the marker (V2, ...) and
rename the symbol with it (_v2, ...) in the patch, ImportMuPDF.cmake and
src/core/MuPdfPatchNotice.cpp.

Dropping it: once upstream MuPDF resolves the outline in one pass, delete
this file and the patch block and html-outline.c hash check in
ImportMuPDF.cmake, src/core/MuPdfPatchNotice.*, its test case, the About
line, and the licence-text note.

